# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) or export in your shell/CI. Everything here is
# PERSONAL: Team IDs, local paths, secrets. Never commit the `.env`. This file
# documents WHICH variables exist; the values below are dummy placeholders.

# Xcode — Apple Development Team ID (10 chars; see Xcode → Settings →
# Accounts → your Apple ID → Membership Details). Confidential: set it in your
# real `.env`, never in branding.json. The Makefile loads `.env`
# automatically and exports DEVELOPMENT_TEAM + APPLE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM (the
# env name the vendored CLI reads), so `make dev-ios-physical` and
# scripts/Xcode/apple-xcode.sh work with zero manual export.
# Simulator builds work ad-hoc without it; only device/archive signing needs it.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=ABCDE12345

# Android SDK — only if not on the default path
# ($HOME/Library/Android/sdk on macOS, $HOME/Android/Sdk on Linux).
# Example:
# ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Library/Android/sdk

# Android release keystore — create it ONCE with keytool. The resulting
# .keystore is PERSONAL (do not commit it: outside the repo or in a secret
# manager). Debug builds sign alone with debug.keystore; for release,
# reference your keystore in the gen/android signingConfigs (autogen).
# Example:
# keytool -genkey -v -keystore $HOME/secrets/release.keystore -alias upload -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000

# Tauri dev host (set by `tauri dev` itself; usually leave alone)
# TAURI_DEV_HOST=192.168.1.10

# App env
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:1420
